{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1474937777,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDgwMzEzNTcyOQ=="},"added":["conference agenda item"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1474968073,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI0OTgxMjE2Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/925#issuecomment-249812167"},"message":"Generally I like the approach to set such \"policies\" to provide a default configuration for `publish` behaviour. But since you mentioned to put this into `create_sibling`: I think this should rather go into `add_sibling` (which is called by `create_sibling`), since this is not about setting up the repo to publish to, but about configuring a remote.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1474973026,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI0OTgzMDA2NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/925#issuecomment-249830064"},"message":"Nope. Because those policies iirc are set per remote within git-annex branch for that remote uuid, ie they are omnipresent across all clones. So you don't want to go flipping them back and forth from different clones - anarchy would come.","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1475161018,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE0OlVubGFiZWxlZEV2ZW50ODA3MTM0NTkx"},"added":[],"removed":["conference agenda item"]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1475869481,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1MjM0NDA2OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/925#issuecomment-252344069"},"message":"Ok, I will address this one by providing `-w,--wanted` which could be either\n- one of the [standard annex groups](https://git-annex.branchable.com/preferred_content/standard_groups/)\n- few of our custom groups\n  - `backup-unrestricted` -- `not metadata=distribution-restrictions=*`\n  - `unique` -- to push derived data (the one present only locally) mostly, but somewhat simplistic since would be just `copies=1` (might consult @joeyh on optimal one).  \n  - `unique-unrestricted` -- as unique but with constrained restriction, which we could advise on while defining a sibling if there is any file with 'distribution-restrictions'\n- and if not matching any of those -- taken as a [preferred content](https://git-annex.branchable.com/preferred_content/) expression  (or should we be kosher and make those separate?  `--wanted-group` and `--wanted` staying more in line with annex?)","files":null}]}